      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Toronto Maple Leafs' summer of reckoning has arrived, and the shock isn't coming from the draft table but from the exit door. <strong>Former goaltender Jack Campbell is walking away from hockey entirely</strong>, a quiet retirement that underscores how quickly the game's fleeting stars vanish once the spotlight fades. The Leafs finished 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points, a season that ended without a playoff berth, but the real story now is roster surgery. Sergei Bobrovsky, a veteran with a pedigree, has agreed to a three-year, $21 million pact, signaling a front-office bet on experience over youth. Meanwhile, the long-rumored departure of Morgan Rielly appears imminent, with insiders insisting he'll leave before the 2026-27 season opens. <strong>The front office must now decide whether to reload around Bobrovsky or pivot hard toward a younger core before free agency's final waves hit.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 20, 2026"
